os-wan-ha-dhcp supplements an existing active/passive OPNsense CARP
cluster so a single DHCP WAN can be attached exclusively to the node that
OPNsense has elected MASTER.

The plugin does not implement a second HA election protocol and does not
replace OPNsense DHCP, routing, NAT, PF, pfsync, or CARP.  It provides a
stable logical WAN abstraction, a shared ordinary unicast MAC identity, and
fail-closed Layer-2 fencing of the local WAN carrier.

This package is experimental.  Production deployment remains gated by
the prototype tests documented in docs/wan-ha-dhcp.md.

